    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.hues\n\n### Description\n\nThis plugin is nice.\r\n\r\nWhen I use `habamax` colorscheme, all display well in `toggleterm`(Fig. 1). \r\n![habamax](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/54238106/4210601a-c60a-4667-bb6c-a0d77966838d)\r\n<p align=\"center\"> Fig. 1 habamax</p>\r\n\r\nBut when I use `mini.hues`, the cursor and the history command(powered by zsh) both can not be displayed in `toggleterm`(Fig. 3).\r\n![mini_hues_noinput](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/54238106/3b1ea043-756b-4d4f-8611-370f7b8277de)\r\n<p align=\"center\"> Fig. 2 minu.hues(when nothing typed)</p>\r\n\r\n![mini_hues](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/54238106/8b74972a-e50a-4d2c-984e-eeac9aba40bc)\r\n<p align=\"center\"> Fig. 3 minu.hues(when just typing ls)</p>\r\n\r\nHope to fix this problem as soon as possible. Sincerely thanks!\r\n\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.9.1\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. My mini.hues config:\r\n ```\r\n {\r\n    \"echasnovski/mini.hues\",\r\n    version = false,\r\n    config = function()\r\n      require(\"mini.hues\").setup({\r\n        background = \"#0E1F25\",\r\n        foreground = \"#c0c8cc\",\r\n        n_hues = 8,\r\n        satuation = \"medium\",\r\n        accent = \"fg\",\r\n        plugin = { default = true },\r\n      })\r\n    end,\r\n  },\r\n```\r\n2. My toggleterm config:\r\n ```\r\n {\r\n    \"akinsho/toggleterm.nvim\",\r\n    version = \"*\",\r\n    keys = {\r\n      { \"<C-\\\\>\", \"<Cmd>execute v:count . 'ToggleTerm '<CR>\", mode = { \"i\", \"n\" } },\r\n    },\r\n    config = true,\r\n    opts = {\r\n      size = 20,\r\n      open_mapping = [[<c-\\>]],\r\n      hide_numbers = true,\r\n      shade_filetypes = {},\r\n      shade_terminals = true,\r\n      shading_factor = 2,\r\n      start_in_insert = true,\r\n      insert_mappings = true,\r\n      persist_size = true,\r\n      direction = \"float\",\r\n      close_on_exit = true,\r\n      shell = vim.o.shell,\r\n      float_opts = {\r\n        border = \"curved\",\r\n        winblend = 0,\r\n        highlights = {\r\n          border = \"Normal\",\r\n          background = \"Normal\",\r\n        },\r\n      },\r\n    },\r\n  },\r\n```\r\n3. I'm using `LazyVim`.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nJust like Fig. 1 above.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\n--------",
